  "slug": "ai-topic-c4ec",
  "summary": "Biological foundation models are now judged by which architectural and input properties bound their performance, not only by aggregate predictive accuracy.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is diagnostic scrutiny of biological foundation models: asking which architectural or input-level properties bound their performance, rather than reporting accuracy alone. BEND 2.0 extends DNA language model evaluation beyond variant effect prediction to sequence design, reporting gains from linear readouts and post-training. An audit of the STATE state-transition decoder for perturbation prediction attributes reliability limits to a low-rank attention bottleneck. In a primary-care EHR transformer for colorectal cancer prediction, performance plateaus at roughly 18 years of time-context, and RoPE positional encoding aliases beyond about 20 years. The new element is the identification of specific structural ceilings, including readout design, decoder rank, and positional encoding range, that constrain what these models can deliver.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-06"
}
